I look at my profile on the website.
I need to change my email address.
Usually, that is quite simple.
I scroll down on the screen.
The instructions on the site are very impersonal.
"Please enter your new email address."
I type the address in carefully.
Then I read the next sentence.
"Please confirm the new email address."
I type it in a second time.
At the bottom of the page it says: "Click here."
I click on the button.
The website loads for a moment.
Now I see a new message.
The text suddenly sounds very official.
"Your data is being checked."
I wait a few seconds.
Then another sentence appears on the screen.
"A code is being sent to your mobile phone."
I hold the mobile phone in my hand and wait for the message.
